<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaColonistPawnKinds.xml                  Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  OWNER'S REQUEST, 2026-08-14: "make a pawntype for the player colonists that is
  MandrakeJawa xenotype and with The Salvation religion."

  🔴 THE HALF THAT A PawnKindDef CANNOT DO, AND WHERE IT LIVES INSTEAD
  ===================================================================
  A `PawnKindDef` carries a XENOTYPE but it cannot carry an IDEOLIGION. There is
  no ideo field on PawnKindDef in 1.6 — a pawn takes the ideo of the FACTION it
  is generated into. So the request splits, and both halves are done:

      xenotype  -> HERE, `xenotypeSet` below.
      religion  -> the PLAYER's ideo is chosen at game start by loading
                   `The Salvation.rid` in the ideoligion browser (committed at
                   `src/Jawa/ideoligion/The Salvation.rid`);
                   the INDIGENOUS tribes get it from their FactionDef, in
                   `../FactionDefs/JawaTribes.xml`.

  ⛔ Do not "fix" this by adding an ideo field to a PawnKindDef. It does not
  exist, and XML that names a field the def does not have fails SILENTLY.

  Two kinds ship here: the colonist proper, and a tribal variant for the
  indigenous Jawa faction so its members are Jawa rather than baseliners.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- The player's starting stock and anything the game generates as "one of
       ours".

       ⚠️ `ParentName` names a def's `Name=` ATTRIBUTE, never its defName. Vanilla
       `Colonist` carries no `Name=`, so it cannot be inherited from — the only
       named ancestor is `BasePlayerPawnKind`, which holds the race/willpower/
       gear-quality half and NOT the apparel money, tags or faction. Those are
       restated here verbatim from Core `PawnKinds_Player.xml`. A ParentName that
       resolves to nothing does not warn: the def is DISCARDED at load. -->
  <PawnKindDef ParentName="BasePlayerPawnKind">
    <defName>Jawa_Colonist</defName>
    <label>Jawa scavenger</label>
    <defaultFactionDef>PlayerColony</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.06</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <apparelTags>
      <li>SaV_apparel_jawa</li>
      <li>ORHermit</li>
      <li>KotORClothing_civilian_hooded</li>
    </apparelTags>
    <!-- 🔴 THE APPAREL IS THE PAWN. SCENARIO_SPEC.md:142 - "All six: xenotype MandrakeJawa,
         apparel locked to the Jawa robe and hood" - and faction_equipment_guidance.md lists
         the Jawa as one of four cases where the silhouette IS the faction. Without these two
         lines a founder arrives in jeans, a t-shirt and a hay sunhat; measured 6 of 6 live on
         2026-08-22 (PLAYER_JAWA_WEARS_JEANS_1) on a kind in exactly this state.
         🔑 `apparelRequired` is generated unconditionally - it ignores both `apparelTags` and
         `apparelMoney` - so the robe and hood always land and `IndustrialBasic` only dresses
         whatever slots they leave open.
         ⚠️ `apparelAllowHeadgearChance` MOVED FROM 0 TO 1 and that is deliberate: the hood is
         headgear, and leaving the roll at 0 is the obvious way to end up with a required hood
         that never appears. -->
    <apparelRequired Inherit="False">
      <li>guy762_Robes_jawa</li>
      <li>guy762_JawaHood</li>
    </apparelRequired>
    <apparelAllowHeadgearChance>1</apparelAllowHeadgearChance>
    <!-- 🔴 apparelMoney 0 — OWNER'S RULING 2026-08-23: "Jawa wear robes+hoods ONLY".
         Asked directly, with this file's own contrary comment in front of him, and he
         chose ONLY. So the random pass gets nothing to spend and a Jawa spawns in the
         robe and the hood and nothing else.
         🔑 This does NOT threaten the robe and hood. PawnApparelGenerator.cs:889 adds
         apparelRequired BEFORE the money loop and independently of it, so they land at
         any budget; 0 only silences the pass that was adding tribal ponchos, kilts and
         war veils on top. Verified against the 1.6 source, not assumed.
         ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-26 by CHECK - "independently of it" is right about MONEY and
         wrong about everything else, and that sentence cost a fortnight. The loop takes
         each required item only when `!workingSet.PairOverlapsAnything(pa)`, so a required
         item whose BODY-PART GROUP is already taken is silently skipped. apparelRequired
         also INHERITS AND APPENDS, parent items FIRST: TribalWarriorBase contributed
         Apparel_WarVeil (FullHead/Overhead) and it ate guy762_JawaHood (UpperHead+Mouth/
         Overhead) on every single spawn - robe 16/16, hood 0/16, measured live. TribalChiefBase
         contributed Apparel_PlateArmor and the Elder lost its ROBE too. RimWorld logged all
         three as `required apparel can't be worn together` on every load.
         ⇒ Inherit="False" on all four, which is just the owner's "robes+hoods ONLY" said in
         XML. ⛔ A PatchOperationRemove cannot reach an inherited <li>.
         ⚠️ Spawn kit only. A Jawa can still craft, buy and wear anything in play. -->
    <apparelMoney>0</apparelMoney>
    <backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>1</backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>
    <techHediffsChance>0.03</techHediffsChance>
    <techHediffsMoney>50~800</techHediffsMoney>
    <techHediffsTags>
      <li>Poor</li>
      <li>Simple</li>
      <li>ImplantEmpireCommon</li>
    </techHediffsTags>
    <techHediffsDisallowTags>
      <li>PainCauser</li>
    </techHediffsDisallowTags>
    <initialResistanceRange>13~21</initialResistanceRange>
    <xenotypeSet>
      <xenotypeChances>
        <MandrakeJawa>1.0</MandrakeJawa>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
      <!-- dusty dark brown — the player's own Jawa -->
    <apparelColor>(77,58,42)</apparelColor>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- The indigenous tribes' rank and file. Tribal parent, not Colonist, so
       they arrive with neolithic-appropriate gear rather than colony kit.
       `TribalWarriorBase` is Core's `Tribal_Warrior` — the tribal melee line.
       `Tribal_Berserker` sits beside it with no `Name=` and cannot be a parent. -->
  <PawnKindDef ParentName="TribalWarriorBase">
    <defName>Jawa_Tribal_Scavenger</defName>
    <label>Jawa scrounger</label>
    <xenotypeSet>
      <xenotypeChances>
        <MandrakeJawa>1.0</MandrakeJawa>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
      <apparelRequired Inherit="False">
      <li>guy762_Robes_jawa</li>
      <li>guy762_JawaHood</li>
    </apparelRequired>
    <!-- 🔴 apparelMoney 0 — OWNER'S RULING 2026-08-23: "Jawa wear robes+hoods ONLY".
         Asked directly, with this file's own contrary comment in front of him, and he
         chose ONLY. So the random pass gets nothing to spend and a Jawa spawns in the
         robe and the hood and nothing else.
         🔑 This does NOT threaten the robe and hood. PawnApparelGenerator.cs:889 adds
         apparelRequired BEFORE the money loop and independently of it, so they land at
         any budget; 0 only silences the pass that was adding tribal ponchos, kilts and
         war veils on top. Verified against the 1.6 source, not assumed.
         ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-26 by CHECK - "independently of it" is right about MONEY and
         wrong about everything else, and that sentence cost a fortnight. The loop takes
         each required item only when `!workingSet.PairOverlapsAnything(pa)`, so a required
         item whose BODY-PART GROUP is already taken is silently skipped. apparelRequired
         also INHERITS AND APPENDS, parent items FIRST: TribalWarriorBase contributed
         Apparel_WarVeil (FullHead/Overhead) and it ate guy762_JawaHood (UpperHead+Mouth/
         Overhead) on every single spawn - robe 16/16, hood 0/16, measured live. TribalChiefBase
         contributed Apparel_PlateArmor and the Elder lost its ROBE too. RimWorld logged all
         three as `required apparel can't be worn together` on every load.
         ⇒ Inherit="False" on all four, which is just the owner's "robes+hoods ONLY" said in
         XML. ⛔ A PatchOperationRemove cannot reach an inherited <li>.
         ⚠️ Spawn kit only. A Jawa can still craft, buy and wear anything in play. -->
    <apparelMoney>0</apparelMoney>
    <apparelTags>
      <li>SaV_apparel_jawa</li>
      <li>ORHermit</li>
      <li>KotORClothing_civilian_hooded</li>
    </apparelTags>
      <!-- Trade Moot tribal roles - the same scavenger economy, lighter -->
    <inventoryOptions>
      <skipChance>0.3</skipChance>
      <subOptionsChooseOne>
        <li><thingDef>MedicineHerbal</thingDef><countRange>1~3</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>Pemmican</thingDef><countRange>8~20</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>Steel</thingDef><countRange>5~15</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>ComponentIndustrial</thingDef><countRange>1~1</countRange></li>
      </subOptionsChooseOne>
    </inventoryOptions>
      <!-- dusty dark brown — Jawa, Trade Moot tribal roles -->
    <apparelColor>(77,58,42)</apparelColor>
      <!-- Trade Moot tribal roles - same clamp as the rest of the Moot. -->
    <forceWeaponQuality>Poor</forceWeaponQuality>
    <maxApparelQuality>Normal</maxApparelQuality>
    <itemQuality>Poor</itemQuality>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="TribalArcherBase">
    <defName>Jawa_Tribal_Slinger</defName>
    <label>Jawa slinger</label>
    <xenotypeSet>
      <xenotypeChances>
        <MandrakeJawa>1.0</MandrakeJawa>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
      <apparelRequired Inherit="False">
      <li>guy762_Robes_jawa</li>
      <li>guy762_JawaHood</li>
    </apparelRequired>
    <!-- 🔴 apparelMoney 0 — OWNER'S RULING 2026-08-23: "Jawa wear robes+hoods ONLY".
         Asked directly, with this file's own contrary comment in front of him, and he
