         any budget; 0 only silences the pass that was adding tribal ponchos, kilts and
         war veils on top. Verified against the 1.6 source, not assumed.
         ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-26 by CHECK - "independently of it" is right about MONEY and
         wrong about everything else, and that sentence cost a fortnight. The loop takes
         each required item only when `!workingSet.PairOverlapsAnything(pa)`, so a required
         item whose BODY-PART GROUP is already taken is silently skipped. apparelRequired
         also INHERITS AND APPENDS, parent items FIRST: TribalWarriorBase contributed
         Apparel_WarVeil (FullHead/Overhead) and it ate guy762_JawaHood (UpperHead+Mouth/
