         contributed Apparel_PlateArmor and the Elder lost its ROBE too. RimWorld logged all
         three as `required apparel can't be worn together` on every load.
         ⇒ Inherit="False" on all four, which is just the owner's "robes+hoods ONLY" said in
         XML. ⛔ A PatchOperationRemove cannot reach an inherited <li>.
         ⚠️ Spawn kit only. A Jawa can still craft, buy and wear anything in play. -->
    <apparelMoney>0</apparelMoney>
    <apparelTags>
      <li>SaV_apparel_jawa</li>
      <li>ORHermit</li>
      <li>KotORClothing_civilian_hooded</li>
    </apparelTags>
      <!-- Trade Moot tribal roles - the same scavenger economy, lighter -->
    <inventoryOptions>
      <skipChance>0.3</skipChance>
      <subOptionsChooseOne>
        <li><thingDef>MedicineHerbal</thingDef><countRange>1~3</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>Pemmican</thingDef><countRange>8~20</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>Steel</thingDef><countRange>5~15</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>ComponentIndustrial</thingDef><countRange>1~1</countRange></li>
      </subOptionsChooseOne>
    </inventoryOptions>
      <!-- dusty dark brown — Jawa, Trade Moot tribal roles -->
    <apparelColor>(77,58,42)</apparelColor>
      <!-- Trade Moot tribal roles - same clamp as the rest of the Moot. -->
    <forceWeaponQuality>Poor</forceWeaponQuality>
    <maxApparelQuality>Normal</maxApparelQuality>
    <itemQuality>Poor</itemQuality>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!-- `weaponTags` IS REQUIRED HERE and on neither sibling. `TribalChiefBase`
       supplies `weaponMoney` 500~1000 but NO `weaponTags` — vanilla's concrete
       `Tribal_ChiefMelee` adds them itself. Inheriting the money with nothing to
       spend it on is a live config error: "weaponMoney is set but weaponTags is
       not". `TribalWarriorBase` and `TribalArcherBase` carry both, so the
       scavenger and the slinger need nothing. Tags copied from
       `Tribal_ChiefMelee`, which is the kind this one stands in for. -->
  <PawnKindDef ParentName="TribalChiefBase">
    <defName>Jawa_Tribal_Elder</defName>
    <label>Jawa clan elder</label>
    <weaponTags>
      <li>NeolithicMeleeAdvanced</li>
      <li>MedievalMeleeAdvanced</li>
    </weaponTags>
    <xenotypeSet>
      <xenotypeChances>
        <MandrakeJawa>1.0</MandrakeJawa>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
      <apparelRequired Inherit="False">
      <li>guy762_Robes_jawa</li>
      <li>guy762_JawaHood</li>
    </apparelRequired>
    <!-- 🔴 apparelMoney 0 — OWNER'S RULING 2026-08-23: "Jawa wear robes+hoods ONLY".
         Asked directly, with this file's own contrary comment in front of him, and he
         chose ONLY. So the random pass gets nothing to spend and a Jawa spawns in the
         robe and the hood and nothing else.
         🔑 This does NOT threaten the robe and hood. PawnApparelGenerator.cs:889 adds
         apparelRequired BEFORE the money loop and independently of it, so they land at
         any budget; 0 only silences the pass that was adding tribal ponchos, kilts and
         war veils on top. Verified against the 1.6 source, not assumed.
         ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-26 by CHECK - "independently of it" is right about MONEY and
         wrong about everything else, and that sentence cost a fortnight. The loop takes
         each required item only when `!workingSet.PairOverlapsAnything(pa)`, so a required
         item whose BODY-PART GROUP is already taken is silently skipped. apparelRequired
         also INHERITS AND APPENDS, parent items FIRST: TribalWarriorBase contributed
         Apparel_WarVeil (FullHead/Overhead) and it ate guy762_JawaHood (UpperHead+Mouth/
         Overhead) on every single spawn - robe 16/16, hood 0/16, measured live. TribalChiefBase
         contributed Apparel_PlateArmor and the Elder lost its ROBE too. RimWorld logged all
         three as `required apparel can't be worn together` on every load.
         ⇒ Inherit="False" on all four, which is just the owner's "robes+hoods ONLY" said in
         XML. ⛔ A PatchOperationRemove cannot reach an inherited <li>.
         ⚠️ Spawn kit only. A Jawa can still craft, buy and wear anything in play. -->
    <apparelMoney>0</apparelMoney>
    <apparelTags>
      <li>SaV_apparel_jawa</li>
      <li>ORHermit</li>
      <li>KotORClothing_civilian_hooded</li>
    </apparelTags>
      <!-- Trade Moot tribal roles - the same scavenger economy, lighter -->
    <inventoryOptions>
      <skipChance>0.3</skipChance>
      <subOptionsChooseOne>
        <li><thingDef>MedicineHerbal</thingDef><countRange>1~3</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>Pemmican</thingDef><countRange>8~20</countRange></li>
        <li><thingDef>Steel</thingDef><countRange>5~15</countRange></li>
